@startuml
' Evidence: Laplace/app/Laplace.Chess/Service/ChessPgnIngestor.cs SHA256 9775995dd88b88edc591f4794d36bd9286fa19f82e85992470867d952e857cca
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFCFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
title Monorepo chess — provider facts and cross-provider identity testimony
start
:Empty input returns; otherwise acquire process-wide ingestion gate;
:Bootstrap distinct provider sources; register canonical-name union;
while (Profile remains?) is (yes)
 :Validate FIDE identifier when applicable;
 :Select source/trust; derive player from FIDE display name or online provider ID;
 :Compose aliases, provider identifier, biography, title, federation, links and ratings;
endwhile (done)
if (Exactly one FIDE profile supplied?) then (yes)
 :For every supplied online profile, compose association context;
 :Attest CORRESPONDS_TO online player to FIDE player under online source;
endif
:Build changes; probe attestation IDs grouped by relation type;
:Suppress already-present testimony; mark changes CountsAsUnit false;
:ApplyMany through shared writer; return profile/player/link counts;
:Release gate in finally;
stop
footer
Source-reviewed orchestration. Nested semantics remain open; no runtime acceptance
claimed. Provider facts are separately witnessed. This method interprets co-supplying
exactly one FIDE profile and online profiles as explicit association; it does not
independently validate that each online profile is the same person. Matching names alone
do not create the association branch. Counts report supplied/planned profiles and links,
not proven novel identities. The presence probe and subsequent shared-writer apply are
separate operations; cross-process race handling belongs to the writer.
end footer

@enduml
